.TH CXREF 1.SH NAMEcxref \- C cross-reference.SH SYNOPSIS\fBcxref\fR[\-x] [\-w=n] [\-t=n] [file].SH DESCRIPTION\fBcxref\fRprints a C source file with numbered lines, and then a cross-reference:every identifier in alphabetical order, followed by the number of eachline it appears on, once for every appearance.  With no file it readsthe standard input..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-x\fRthe cross-reference only, headed\fBCross Reference for \fIfile\fR,\fRwithout the listing..TP 12\fB\-w=\fIn\fRlines\fIn\fRcharacters wide, more than 50; 132 unless told..TP 12\fB\-t=\fIn\fRidentifiers significant to\fIn\fRcharacters, between 8 and 24; 24 unless told..SH EXAMPLES.nfcxref prog.c > prog.xref      listing and cross-referencecxref -x -w=80 prog.c         the cross-reference, for a narrow screen.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOcb, ctags, xrf